                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "16bit Trader is not a game about trading. Buy/sell prices for goods seem to be random and travel is so expensive that you'll always make an overall loss from trading. Taking randomly-appearing quests and gathering once-per-day diamonds are the only reliable way to make money.\n\nIt's a lazy port of a mobile game. It's designed around a-few-minutes-a-day casual play, but it doesn't hold up well when you sit down to seriously play it. Don't bother.",
